---
// Hardware reality vs Big-O notation: small N slice scan vs hash table & pointer-chasing stalls.
const W = 900;
const H = 286;
---
<figure class="gect">
  <div class="gect-scroll">
    <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Comparison explaining why Big-O ignores CPU cache constants, comparing contiguous slice scanning against pointer-heavy structures on small to medium N.">
      {/* Left card: Asymptotic Big-O blind spot */}
      <rect x="14" y="14" width="440" height="258" rx="10" class="gect-card" />
      <text x="30" y="42" class="gect-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>1. Asymptotic O(1) vs real hardware latency constants</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>1. Độ phức tạp O(1) vs hằng số độ trễ phần cứng thật</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="60" width="408" height="62" rx="6" class="gect-box is-ok" />
      <text x="44" y="81" class="gect-b-ok">O(N) slice scan (16 ints = 128B = 2 cache lines)</text>
      <text x="44" y="101" class="gect-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Prefetched in L1 (~1 ns/step). Measured Apple M2: 5.4 ns/op!</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>CPU nạp tuyến tính L1 (~1 ns/bước). Đo Apple M2: 5.4 ns/op!</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="136" width="408" height="62" rx="6" class="gect-box" />
      <text x="44" y="157" class="gect-b">O(1) hash map vs linked list / unpooled pointers</text>
      <text x="44" y="177" class="gect-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Map lookup jumps from ~4.5 ns hot to 80–200 ns on cache miss.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Map băm + nhảy con trỏ vọt từ ~4.5 ns lên 80–200 ns khi lớn.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="30" y="210" width="408" height="46" rx="6" class="gect-box is-red" />
      <text x="44" y="230" class="gect-b-red">Why Big-O misleads: c1=1ns vs c2=100ns DRAM miss</text>
      <text x="44" y="247" class="gect-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Contiguous O(N log N) slice sort beats pointer binary trees.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Sort mảng liền khối O(N log N) thắng áp đảo cây con trỏ.</tspan>
      </text>

      {/* Right card: Production N boundary decision rule */}
      <rect x="470" y="14" width="416" height="258" rx="10" class="gect-card" />
      <text x="486" y="42" class="gect-h">
        <tspan data-lang-en>2. RAER rule: fix realistic production input N first</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>2. Luật RAER: chốt kích thước dữ liệu N thật trước</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="486" y="60" width="384" height="60" rx="6" class="gect-box" />
      <text x="500" y="81" class="gect-b">Small fixed N (&le; 16–32 items): Headers / Tags</text>
      <text x="500" y="101" class="gect-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Linear slice stays on Stack: 0 GC allocs vs map heap cost.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Slice nhỏ nằm trên Stack: 0 alloc Heap, nhanh hơn map mới.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="486" y="132" width="384" height="60" rx="6" class="gect-box" />
      <text x="500" y="153" class="gect-b">Large N (&ge; 1,000+ lookups) or streaming 10 GB logs</text>
      <text x="500" y="173" class="gect-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Pre-sized SwissTable or fixed streaming buf wins at scale.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>SwissTable dựng sẵn hoặc buffer streaming cố định mới tối ưu.</tspan>
      </text>

      <rect x="486" y="204" width="384" height="52" rx="6" class="gect-box is-ok" />
      <text x="500" y="225" class="gect-b-ok">Efficiency = Value / Resource Cost (CPU + RAM + Lat)</text>
      <text x="500" y="244" class="gect-m">
        <tspan data-lang-en>Measure real N under go test -bench before guessing Big-O.</tspan>
        <tspan data-lang-vi>Đo thực tế trên đúng kích thước N trước khi đoán bằng Big-O.</tspan>
      </text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Asymptotic Big-O hides hardware cache constants, allocation cost, and GC pauses. On small real-world N (like HTTP headers or tenant IDs), a stack-resident slice beats allocating a map cleanly; on massive datasets, data locality dominates everything.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Ký hiệu Big-O bỏ qua hằng số cache CPU, chi phí cấp phát và GC. Với N nhỏ thực tế (vài chục HTTP header hay config tag), quét slice liền khối trên Stack vượt xa việc cấp phát Map; còn với dữ liệu lớn, tính cục bộ bộ nhớ vẫn quyết định tất cả.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .gect { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .gect-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .gect svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 660px; height: auto; }
  .gect text { font-size: 12px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .gect-card { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .gect-box { fill: var(--bg); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .gect-box.is-red { stroke: var(--red); fill: var(--red-tint-bg); }
  .gect-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gect-box.is-ok { stroke: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gect-h { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gect-b { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .gect-b-red { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .gect-b-ok { font-weight: 700; fill: rgb(21, 128, 61); }
  :global(html[data-theme='dark']) .gect-b-ok { fill: rgb(74, 222, 128); }
  .gect-m { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 11px; }
  .gect figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
